course: dictionary
lesson: 11918
title: A place called a cafe
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: A cafe is a place where you can buy something to eat or drink. Look at the clues in the sentence to work out what kind of place it is. «Ben bought a cup of tea and a cheese sandwich at the cafe.» He bought food and a drink, so a cafe must be a place that sells them.
explain: Some words sound like a place you already know, but a cafe is smaller and simpler than a big restaurant. «The family sat at a cafe table by the window and ordered hot chocolate.» The table and the ordering tell you people sit down there and are served.
explain: The word can also be part of another name. «An internet cafe has computers, and people pay to use them.» Here the word internet tells you the cafe is about computers, not only food. The first word helps you understand the second.
fact: A cafe is a small restaurant where people buy drinks and simple meals.
fact: Drinks in a cafe can include tea, coffee and juice, and simple meals can include sandwiches and cakes.
fact: An internet cafe is a place where people pay to use computers.
fact: The word can also be written as «café» with an accent, and «cafes» or «cafés» is the plural, meaning more than one.
exercise: «Ben bought a cup of tea and a cheese sandwich at the cafe.» Where did Ben buy his lunch? | At a library | At a train station | At a football pitch | * At a cafe
exercise: Nadia went to an internet cafe to use a computer. What is an internet cafe? | A place where people buy cakes and tea only | A library full of books | A school for young children | * A place where people pay to use computers
exercise: Find and copy one word that means a place where people buy drinks and simple meals. | hot | * cafe | window | table
test: «Maya paid for her juice at the cafe counter.» What did Maya buy? | A pair of shoes | A bus ticket | A new coat | * A drink
test: Which word means a small restaurant where you can buy tea and cakes? | Museum | * Cafe | Park | Station
exam: «The family sat at a cafe table and shared a plate of cakes.» Where did the family sit? | In a school hall | * At a table in a cafe | In a swimming pool | On a bus
